# The reference checks m, the service others depend on, once more a
# second after results of those that depend on it came in (at 11.0 s),
# and counts its interval from there. checkd does not: when the
# reference does this is not found out yet. So m itself is checked at
# other times, and recovers a second earlier. What this scenario is
# about, who notifies while m is CRITICAL and who does not, is compared.
ignore m checked at other times: see above
ignore n-ann-a-m follows m
ignore-log a;m follows m
